# A mine that goes after an enemy, looked at as it goes (a tester's picture: "one of my mines became an oval", the mine
# lying between them and the boss, where an armed mine seeks its target; mines.sim only looks at mines lying still).
# QUEST_SIM_GIVE=17 QUEST_SIM_HOLD=17 QUEST_SIM_NEAR=427 QUEST_SIM_NEAR_AT=6,0 QUEST_ROWS_TRACE=74 on Eudora (--level 4):
# a Blarg trooper 6 units ahead (Y at 1150 skips the arrival movie; Ratchet is put there about frame 1990). On Novalis
# the critters run into the mine before it is armed, from 6 units and from 12, and it goes off at once (round in the air
# and lying, in those shots). A mine is taken into the glove and lobbed about three units ahead; 120 ticks after the
# release it is armed and seeks the nearest enemy in reach (the game's sequences 1 and 2, hopping). The shots are to be
# looked at: is it round as it flies, lies and puts its spikes out? 0.1.18 on PC: "rows ... (even)", lean 0.000, round in
# the air, lying and with its spikes out; it went off by the trooper as it armed, so it was not seen hopping.
